# Copy to .env and fill in. Nothing here is read from a real gateway until you do.

# Optional. Left unset, the SDK asks https://agentgateway-mcp.neuraltrust.ai,
# which finds your gateway from the key. Set it for NeuralTrust's development
# environment, or for a Hybrid gateway, whose own data plane is the only one
# that serves it: the MCP host that plane is published on, and nothing after it.
# TRUSTGATE_URL=https://agentgateway-mcp.dev.neuraltrust.ai

# The API key of the application you want to run as. Issued from the
# Authentication block of its General tab, and shown once. Each application has
# its own: changing which application an example runs against means changing
# this, not just creating one. `uv run whoami.py` says which one a key reaches.
TRUSTGATE_API_KEY=<your-trustgate-api-key>

# user_agent.py runs as you, not as an application, and needs no API key above.
# Your personal key from the Portal (Personal key) is all it takes:
TRUSTGATE_PERSONAL_KEY=<your-personal-key>
# Or, without one, it signs in through your browser to your Store's MCP URL, as
# the console shows it where the Store is added to an MCP client.
# TRUSTGATE_STORE_URL=https://your-gateway.mcp.neuraltrust.ai/store/mcp

# end_user_agent.py and user_agent.py always need this: it calls Anthropic directly. batch.py
# needs it only when your key reaches no LLM consumer, since it prefers to send
# the model call through the gateway like everything else.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=<your-anthropic-api-key>

# Same story for framework_mcp.py, which calls an OpenAI model: only needed when
# your key reaches no LLM consumer.
OPENAI_API_KEY=<your-openai-api-key>

# Optional. Set these only when one key reaches more than one consumer of the
# same plane — the SDK then says so and asks which.
# TRUSTGATE_MCP_CONSUMER=
# TRUSTGATE_LLM_CONSUMER=
